cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cylie: certificates, configurations, and a standalone exact-arithmetic verifier for cylinder insertions and expansions"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/maticivan/cylie"
authors:
  - family-names: "Matić"
    given-names: "Ivan"
    affiliation: "Baruch College, City University of New York"
  - family-names: "Radoičić"
    given-names: "Radoš"
    affiliation: "Baruch College, City University of New York"
  - family-names: "Spomer"
    given-names: "Andreas"
    affiliation: "Universität zu Köln"
keywords:
  - cylinder packing
  - kissing configurations
  - sum-of-squares certificates
  - semidefinite programming
  - computer-assisted proof
  - exact arithmetic
abstract: >-
  Data and standalone verifier for the computer-assisted proofs in the paper
  "Insertion and expansion of cylinders around the unit ball" by I. Matić,
  R. Radoičić and A. Spomer. The repository contains rational certificates
  showing that no more than n non-overlapping cylinders of the stated radii
  can touch the unit ball for n = 4, 5, 6, 7, explicit rational
  configurations for the insertion results, and the verifier cylie, which
  checks all of them in exact arithmetic.
